APACHE SPARK vs HADOOP MAPREDUCE
(the shift that changes big data forever)

MAP REDUCE
- washing 1 plate, drying it, putting it away, then picking up the next plate. 
- disk based processing ( slow & disk I/O heavy)
- supports only batch
- every step - disk  i/o - slow
-- read -> process -> write to disk -> read again -> process -> write to disk. 

SPARK
- loading the entire dishwasher, running one cycle & everything gets done. 
- in-memory processing ( fast & efficient)
- batch + streaming
- everything in memory = 100 x faster
- read -> trans -> trans-> write final o/p
- built in ML libraries
- databricks - managed spark with zero infra handover. 

WHY IS SPARK FASTER THEN MR (Map Reduce) ?
spark is fatser because :
- it processes data in memory (RAM) instead of writing intermediate results to disk.
- it has an optimized execution engine
- it supports in-memory caching.

