OPTIMIZE
-------
- used to compact small files into larger ones to reduce fragmentation & improve query perf.
- when combined with z-order --> it also combines data based on a specified cols (enabling faster data skipping & more
efficient query execution)
- OPTIMIZE BRONZE.CLAIMS
ZORDER BY MEMBER_ID
- it physically co-locates related data in the same files based on col vlaues. 
- in delta lake solves the small files prob using bin-packing
- internally, it rewrites many small parquet files into fewer larger files 
& updates the delta trans log w/o modifying files in place.

Z-ORDER
------
- is a  multi dimensional clustering mechanism
- instead of simple sorting, delta converts col values into morton/ z order values by interleaving
bits & physically co-locates related rows. 
- this improves file level data skipping because delta stores min/max statistics for each file
- queries scan fewer files when filtering on zorder cols. 
- avoid zorder on low cardinality cols
- for newer databricks workloads, liquid clustering is often preferred over manual zorder. 

LIQUID CLUSTERING
--------------------
- is an evolution of zorder in databricks
- instead of manually running optimize zorder, we define clustering keys & databricks incrementally data 
locality automatically. 
- it avoids rigid partitions, reduces full table rewrites & works better for large frequently updated delta table. 


VACUUM
------
- is a maintenance command in delta lake used to permanently delete old, unneeded old data files from storage. 
- it helps control storage cost & remove obsolete files that are no longer part of the current table state. 
- in delta lake, data is never over written in place
when you update, delete, merge , optimize
- delta creates new files & marks old one as "no longer active" in the trans log. 

WHAT VACUUM DOES
---------------
- scans delta trans log
- identifies files not referenced by current table state.
- delte those files from storage. 

RETENTION ( 7 days)
- delta lake keeps olf diles for :
- supports time travel
- supports streaming consistency
- prevents accidental deletion of active data. 

HOW VACUUM WORKS INTERNALLY
- reads delta trans log (_delta_log)
- identifies 
-- actvie files (current versions)
-- deleted files (old versions)
- compares against retention threshold. 
- deletes files from storage. 
without vaccum:
- table updated daily.
- after 1 month :
- 100 GB active data
- 900GB old files.
- total storage : 1 TB. 

PERFORMANCE BETWEEN DELTA LAKE CDF vs MERGE OPERATION
-----------------------------------------------------
CDF & MERGE - are not direct alternatives - they solve diff problems & are usually used together in modern delta lake pipeline. 
CDF - change data feed
- used to capture only incremental changes in a delta table such as insert, update, delete. 
- with CDF, I can read only changed rows b/w delta versioning using readChangeFeed = value, so instead of processing 
the full dataset. process only inc records.
- CDF -- doesn't replace merge

MERGE
- used to apply those changes to a target delta table using upsert logic.
- for a perf perspective - the major diff is the amt of data processed.
- if we use merge alone, spark may need to scan a large portion of the src & tgt table. perf join, shuffle & rewrite
affected files.
- if I have a 500 million row table, only 10k rows changed, merge w/o incremental logic may still process a significant 
amt of data. 

EXPLAIN HOW SPARK TUNGSTEN ENGINE IMPROVES EXECUTION THROUGH OFF HEAP MEMORY & WHOLE CODE GENERATION
OFF HEAP MEMORY
- stores data outside JVM heap in a compact binary format, reducing garbage collection overhead & improving memory efficiency.

WHOLE CODE GENERATION
- dynamically generate optimized java bytecode by combining multiple operators into a single execution path,
reducing function call overhead & intermediate obj creation.
- together these optimizations
- improves CPU utilization
- memory management
- overall spark execution perf. 















